WEBVTT

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:07.020
"Touken Ranbu Hanamaru S2"

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.980
Did something happen
to Ookurikara and the others?

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.070
From what Master said,

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:15.860
the strength of Ookurikara and the others
dispatched to Edo has become weakened.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:16.870
What did you say?

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.870
For that group to have trouble...

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.950
I don't know how that could be, either.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.040
Master's power can't bring them home?

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.290
Apparently, right now,

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:30.920
they're standing off against the enemy
while protecting Date Munemura.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.970
If they are brought back right now,
then history will definitely be altered.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:40.010
But if something happens
to them because of that...

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:43.930
However, that is the fate of a Sword Warrior.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:47.270
Damn it! Can't anything be done?

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:48.860
Can't we send reinforcements or something?

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:52.070
But only one team can be
sent to each time period

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:54.110
with the same space-time transportation device.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.070
Can we use the old one?

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:01.950
This citadel has another one, doesn't it?

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:07.000
"Sealed | Sa | Sealed"

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:06.120
Then that one might be able to send
a group to the same time period, right?

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:07.210
That's it!

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:08.380
That's no good.

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:11.590
There is no precedent,
so we don't know what could happen.

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:15.720
That doesn't mean we can
just wait around here, does it?

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.590
I want to save them...

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:20.430
I want to save our friends from this citadel!

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:23.930
Very well.

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:26.230
I will go talk to the <i>saniwa</i>.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:33.190
The <i>saniwa </i>has given permission
for a team to be dispatched.

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:43.790
"Sa"

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:36.820
However, only three swords may go.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:42.240
The destination will be
August 14, 1747, Edo Castle.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.200
Those being dispatched are...

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.460
Tantou, Aizen Kunitoshi!

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.170
I'm itching to use my skills!

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:50.290
Tantou, Atsushi Toushirou!

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:51.670
Leave it to me!

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:54.050
Finally, the captain will be...

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:56.170
Uchigatana, Kashuu Kiyomitsu!

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:57.340
Roger.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:02.510
Master said the only one they could entrust to
be captain in this predicament is you, Kashuu.

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:05.520
I guess that means I'm loved, huh?

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.980
I will definitely save everyone.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:12.310
It is unclear how long you
will be able to stay over there.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:15.480
You should assume that you won't
be able to stay for very long.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.610
We'll be off, then.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.950
Kashuu, Atsushi, Aizen.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:24.620
Make sure you come back. All of you.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.700
We await your return.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:48.480
All right, let's go!

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:16.170
Why are you people trying
so hard to protect me, a stranger?

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:20.130
It's true that I have no relationship with you.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:24.760
But if you live, then my
relationships will be protected.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:26.010
What do you mean?

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:28.060
Just talking to myself.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:31.600
In any case, we have
something we must protect.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:32.980
That's why...

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:37.780
...those who try to stop us deserve
to die a thousand times over!

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:43.070
At least have the grace to die elegantly!

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.250
I've repaid my debt.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.210
Thanks, you saved me.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:02.930
Fresh troops, huh?

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:06.430
Of all things, they just have to
keep sending the tough enemies, huh?

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.850
Oh no, my clothes...

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:13.100
Does this mean I've been driven into a corner?

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:17.190
Take that!

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:23.610
That scampering about's irritating!

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:37.790
Kashuu-<i>san</i>?

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:39.210
--Aizen!
--Atsushi!

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.050
How did you...?

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.670
We'll tell you all about it later!

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:44.760
We'll hold them back here.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:48.180
So you guys take those people
and get away from the castle!

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.300
But...

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.970
We are Sword Warriors.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:54.600
It is our duty to protect history, right?

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:59.060
But we also definitely
don't want anyone to break.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:03.190
Kashuu.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:05.740
I leave it to you.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:07.110
Yeah.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:17.960
Will Kashuu and the others be okay?

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:20.130
I'm sure they'll be fine.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.880
Let's believe in them.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.180
Is this the last of them?

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:33.350
They were pretty strong opponents.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:34.980
Kashuu, Aizen.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:37.690
It looks like we're not finished yet.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:45.860
What is that guy?

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.860
Another new enemy?

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.240
Who knows? But...

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:00.130
...it doesn't look like it'll
let us go home without a fight.

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:21.190
These guys are tough...

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:23.820
It'll be hard to take
them on with just three of us.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:25.230
If only...

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.440
If only we had one more...

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:32.660
Yasusada?!

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.540
Ow...

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.500
Huh? Kiyomitsu?

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.460
In the first place, where am I...?

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:46.340
What are these guys?

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:47.590
Dunno.

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:49.720
But we don't have time to talk.

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:01.650
We just have to kill those guys, right?

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:08.820
We'll finish it...

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:10.240
...with this!

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:16.700
You were pretty good.

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:20.250
You, too. You got stronger, huh?

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:28.630
Let's go!

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:30.510
Atsushi!

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:31.930
Right!

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:42.350
Just one left!

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.320
Kiyomitsu!

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:01.210
--Kashuu!
--Yamatonokami!

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:17.850
Those who see my bare skin...

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:19.430
...will die!

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:23.480
Come, our fight to the death starts now!

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:35.320
I think we finished them off somehow.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:37.410
It doesn't look like there are any enemies left.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:41.080
Man, I'm exhausted.

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:45.420
Welcome back, Yasusada.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:47.420
Thanks, Kiyomitsu.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:50.920
Jeez, where have you
been for so long, anyway?

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:54.130
Well, it's a long story...

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:57.010
If it's a long story, then let's
take our time hearing it back home.

00:08:57.010 --> 00:09:00.930
I want to hear all the details
of the heroic acts on your journey!

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:03.850
Then, shall we get back to the citadel?

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:04.850
Yeah.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:08.270
Huh?

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:09.940
I don't have my transportation device...

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:10.690
What?!

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:12.860
I might've dropped it while I was fighting.

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:16.660
Oh, there it is! But...

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:19.120
Does it still work...?

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:22.290
It won't move...

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:23.750
What?!

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:26.080
Huh? I didn't push anything...

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:27.790
We must've reached our limit.

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:28.960
Oh, no!

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:30.710
Yasusada!

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:33.710
It's okay! I'll be right behind you!

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:36.300
Yasusada!

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.890
I'll definitely go home!

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:44.930
"April"

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:49.400
"Clear Mirror, Still Water"

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:14.880
What...?

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:36.690
Yasusada!

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:39.150
Kiyomitsu!

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:41.490
You surprised me,
coming back all of a sudden like that!

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:45.290
Well, I'm not sure how I got back, either.

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:46.830
Jeez...

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:50.370
Welcome back for real this time, Yasusada.

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:52.330
Thanks, Kiyomitsu.

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:54.710
Looks like I kept you waiting a long time.

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:57.630
What?!

00:10:57.090 --> 00:11:01.340
"Repair Room"
"1 Yamatonokami"

00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:00.840
It's been four months
since the fight at Edo Castle?!

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:02.760
Yeah.

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:08.230
But I left right after you did...

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:12.270
Your device was broken, so maybe
the coordinates didn't match up properly.

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:14.230
I see...

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:17.070
Well? Since you left for
your journey the year before last,

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:20.320
where have you been, and what've
you been doing this whole time?

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:24.990
I didn't think it'd take this long, either.

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:27.580
In order to not interfere with history,

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:29.790
I would watch a certain period for a few days,

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:33.630
then jump to a few years later, and repeat.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:36.670
I wanted to see properly with my own eyes...

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:39.340
Okita-<i>kun</i>'s final moments.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:41.130
You...

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:43.550
Even when Okita-<i>kun</i> was suffering,

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:47.810
I would think of Master and everyone
waiting at the citadel as I watched.

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:51.520
Kondo-<i>san</i>, Hijikata-<i>san</i>,
and Okita-<i>kun</i> all passed away,

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:54.230
and even the Shinsengumi met its end.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:12:01.320
But I visited the next period,
and the one after that,

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:03.910
and the one beyond that.

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:05.240
"The one beyond"?

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:06.950
Yeah.

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:09.330
Even after the age of swords ended,

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:14.170
there were times of war and peace.

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:17.420
The world really changed in a dizzying way.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:21.130
In just a few decades, it was hard
to believe that it was the same country.

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:22.300
Really.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:25.140
But no matter how many decades passed,

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:27.010
no matter how much the world changed,

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:32.480
the story of Okita-<i>kun</i> and the
Shinsengumi continued to be passed down.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:35.560
That's why I thought...

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:41.610
The history that we Sword Warriors
are protecting is so precious!

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:47.280
Of course, I knew it was important.

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:50.120
But after going on this journey,

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:54.670
I was able to experience
deeply the real reason we fight.

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:56.000
I see.

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:02.380
You became stronger,
just like you promised, huh?

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:03.420
Yeah.

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:09.810
I want to fulfill my duties again here
at this citadel, with Master and everyone.

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:14.640
That reminds me, why did you
suddenly show up at Edo Castle?

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:16.560
Oh, that was...

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:23.190
Hm?

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:26.280
Huh? What?!

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:38.710
This is...

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:09.490
Are you finished helping Master?

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:12.700
Yeah. Master is quite a handful.

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:14.750
Have you gotten used to your human body yet?

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:22.750
Not completely, but I never dreamed
that I would ever be able to move as I wished.

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:26.050
It's nice being able
to go where you want, isn't it?

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:28.470
Hasebe-<i>san</i>!

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:30.800
I broke another plate!

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:32.970
How many do you have
to break before you're satisfied?

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:34.100
Are you hurt?

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:37.690
I'm fine. But dinner is...

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:39.690
Jeez, I can't leave it to you.

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:43.690
Listen, I'll take care of Master's
daily necessities starting today.

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:46.320
Hey! It's not fair for you to hog it all!

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:49.860
Kashuu, you don't like doing
work that gets you dirty, right?

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:51.740
That's true, but...

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:54.080
There are times when
preparing food gets you dirty.

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:56.370
That's why I will do it.

00:14:56.370 --> 00:15:00.250
It'll be a big help if
Hasebe-<i>san</i> does the cooking, huh?

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:04.670
Well, we're the only ones
at this citadel right now,

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:06.670
so we all have a lot to do.

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:09.340
It's a little lonely since it's so big.

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:11.300
I wish Iwatooshi could be here, too.

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:12.590
Who's Iwatooshi?

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:14.970
Musashibou Benkei's naginata.

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:18.430
We protected Lord Yoshitsune together.

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:21.770
Is there a sword like that for you, Kashuu-<i>san</i>?

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:26.030
There is. I was a favorite sword
of Okita Souji from the Shinsengumi.

00:15:26.030 --> 00:15:28.190
Oh, I see.

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:32.030
If another of the Shinsengumi
or Okita-<i>kun</i>'s swords manifests,

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:34.580
then I'd have a lot to talk about.

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:36.740
I hope one arrives soon.

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:38.450
Yeah.

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:56.430
I have to return quickly to
my normal time where everyone's waiting.

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:19.540
The cherry blossoms are...!

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:21.410
Huh? What?

00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:31.260
The next thing I knew, I was at Edo Castle.

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:35.840
What's with those cherry blossoms?

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:38.600
They're very mysterious, aren't they?

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:43.480
What did you do while I was gone, Kiyomitsu?

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:45.350
Well, a lot happened.

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:49.610
We got a bunch of new Sword Warriors. And...

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:03.540
What?

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:06.580
You also got stronger
like you promised, Kiyomitsu.

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:08.210
Of course I did!

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:11.300
I can't lose to you.

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:15.550
Let's become stronger
together from now on, too.

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:19.010
What are you talking about?

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:24.850
I'll get even stronger than you, Yasusada.

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:36.200
"Spirit, Technique, Strength"

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:43.200
Your sword has gotten heavier, Kiyomitsu.

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:47.460
I was training hard
while you were gone, Yasusada.

00:17:58.140 --> 00:17:58.840
Kiyomitsu.

00:17:58.840 --> 00:17:59.970
Hm?

00:18:01.060 --> 00:18:04.220
Let's spar again tomorrow.

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:07.850
Of course.

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:12.900
You didn't put any decorations up, huh?

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:15.490
We just changed rooms recently.

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.860
Then, let's do it together later.

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:21.950
You're not ready yet?
Everyone's probably tired of waiting.

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:23.790
Wait a sec.

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:26.580
It's been a while since I saw everyone...

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:28.250
Here.

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:31.250
Oh, you fixed it for me!

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:36.220
I had time on my hands while
you were gone, so I decorated it.

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:42.640
Thanks for waiting!

00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:45.020
Yamatonokami!

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:47.310
Y-Yamatonokami-<i>san</i>!

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:48.390
I'm back.

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:49.810
Welcome home!

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:52.440
You seem like you're doing well!

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:53.770
Yeah.

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:58.740
I am Kashuu Kiyomitsu.

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:01.620
I was the first sword
to manifest at this citadel,

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:06.540
and I fulfill my duty as a
Sword Warrior with my many friends.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:09.210
That is what is expected of me.

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:11.670
That's why...

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:15.090
I'm counting on you from now on, too.

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:20.430
Oh, it looks like the cherry blossoms
have answered you.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.680
There are so many of you!

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:27.020
I'll take a test picture first!

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:29.850
Everyone, smile!

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:32.730
Let's see.

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:36.440
Oh, that was good.
This is a pretty good pic, too.

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:37.570
Everyone!

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:39.650
Oh, they're finally here, huh?

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:41.450
Sorry for being late!

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:46.790
The <i>saniwa</i> wanted to talk to the
Sword Warriors who manifested last year.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:49.200
Next is the real thing!

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:50.910
Everyone ready?

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:53.170
Yes!

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:54.710
Smile!

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:09.480
Hey, don't you think this is a little <i>too</i> cute?

00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:11.100
It's fine, isn't it?

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:13.150
I think it looks good on you.

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:15.150
I wonder...

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:18.610
If you don't make yourself cute,
Master won't take care of you.

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:23.450
Isn't it a little too flashy?

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:25.570
All right, I'm done.

00:23:45.520 --> 00:23:50.610
"This anime <i>was</i> about
the stories of the <i>Hanamaru</i> days

00:23:50.610 --> 00:23:54.330
of a certain group of
Sword Warriors in a certain citadel."

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:01.500
"Let's <i>Hanamaru</i> After This, Too!!"
